146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The Bluestock Mutual Fund Analytics project focuses on analysing mutual fund data to understand fund performance, investor behaviour, SIP trends, and portfolio risk. The project combines data cleaning, exploratory data analysis, financial analytics, and interactive Power BI dashboards to provide useful insights for investors and fund analysis. The analysis was performed using mutual fund master data, NAV history, fund performance data, SIP inflows, investor transactions, and portfolio holdings. Python and Pandas were used for data cleaning, transformation, exploratory analysis, and advanced analytics. Power BI was used to develop an interactive dashboard consisting of multiple analytical pages. The project evaluated important performance and risk metrics such as returns, volatility, Sharpe ratio, maximum drawdown, Value at Risk \(VaR\), Conditional Value at Risk \(CVaR\), and sector concentration using the Herfindahl-Hirschman Index \(HHI\). Investor analysis included cohort analysis and SIP continuation analysis to identify investment patterns and investors who may be at risk of discontinuing their SIPs. A simple fund recommendation model was also developed to identify the top-performing funds by Sharpe ratio according to the investor's risk category. The Power BI dashboard provides interactive visualizations for industry trends, fund performance, investor analytics, SIP inflows, market trends, and fund-level NAV analysis. Overall, the project demonstrates how financial data analytics can be used to evaluate mutual fund performance, identify investment and concentration risks, understand investor behaviour, and support data-driven investment analysis)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
